<<<
In the first place, there is no doubt about the numeral pronoun one; its possessive, reflexive, & deputy pronoun, are never one’s, oneself, & one, but always the corresponding parts of he, she, or it.
===
In the first place, there is no doubt about the numeral pronoun *one*; its possessive, reflexive, & deputy pronoun, are never *one's*, *oneself*, & *one*, but always the corresponding parts of *he*, *she*, or *it*.
>>>

<<<
I saw one drop his stick; Certainly, if one offers herself as candidate; One would not go off even when I hammered it.
===
*I saw one drop* his *stick*; *Certainly, if one offers* herself *as candidate*; *One would not go off even when* I *hammered* it.
>>>
